=== Climate ===
Tochigi Prefecture has a tropical monsoon climate with highland modification (Köppen ''Am''), influenced by its elevated interior terrain. The Tochigi Basin, at 400–600 m elevation, experiences slightly cooler temperatures than the surrounding coastal lowlands, with more pronounced diurnal temperature variation. The Asuka highlands, above 1,000 m, experience a subtropical highland climate with significantly cooler nights and frequent fog, particularly during the winter dry season.

The landlocked position creates a rain shadow effect in the Tochigi Basin, which receives less precipitation than the coastal prefectures. The wet season (November–April) brings monsoon rains that are partially intercepted by the surrounding mountain ranges, while the dry season (May–October) is characterised by clear skies, cool nights, and morning fog in the valley floors—conditions that are ideal for both tea cultivation and lacquerware curing.

